{
  "id": "pressure_coefficient",
  "title": "Pressure Coefficient",
  "description": "The Pressure Coefficient is the ratio of pressure forces to inertial forces. It is an important parameter in most fluid flow applications.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Pressure Coefficient Formula\n\nThe pressure coefficient is the ratio of _pressure forces_ to _inertial forces_ and can be expressed as:\n\n**Cp = dP / (ρ v² / 2)**\n\nOr alternatively:\n\n**Cp = dh (ρ v² / 2 g)**\n\n### Where:\n- **Cp** = pressure coefficient (dimensionless)\n- **dP** = pressure difference (Pa or N/m²)\n- **ρ** = fluid density (kg/m³)\n- **v** = flow velocity (m/s)\n- **dh** = head (m)\n- **g** = acceleration of gravity (9.81 m/s²)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "pressure_diff",
          "label": "Pressure Difference (dP)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "fluid_density",
          "label": "Fluid Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "flow_velocity",
          "label": "Flow Velocity (v)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 5
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "pressure_coefficient",
          "label": "Pressure Coefficient (Cp)",
          "formula": "inputs.pressure_diff / (inputs.fluid_density * inputs.flow_velocity ** 2 / 2)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
